@jinzhen-lin @BBuf 
A small load-time memory fix for the Humming MoE path. The tensors that transform_humming_layer replaces stay stranded in the caching allocator. On DeepSeek-V4.1-Flash with TP-sharded experts that costs 7–19 GB per GPU, and TP4 does not start at the default --mem-fraction-static. The MXFP4 MoE path and the FP8 HIP int4 path already call torch.cuda.empty_cache() after replacing their weights. This PR does the same after each Humming sublayer and adds a CPU unit test.

Could you take a look when you have time?

